DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Feast of the Dormition at Kefali\, Kalamos
LOCATION:Kefali (Porto Leone)\, Kalamos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The abandoned village of Kefali at Kalamos's southern cape comes alive once a year: festive vespers with artoklasia at 7:30pm on 14 August and a hierarchical liturgy on the morning of the 15th at the church of Agioi Anargyroi\, with the Metropolitan of Lefkada\, pilgrims arriving by boat from Mytikas and Kalamos village\, and a treat offered afterwards. There is no road\; arrange a boat from Kalamos port or Mytikas the day before.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kalamos/#kefali-porto-leone-feast-of-the-dormition-at-kefali-kalamos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kalamos/#kefali-porto-leone-feast-of-the-dormition-at-kefali-kalamos
END:VEVENT
